The following auxiliary estimates use the directly indexed extended-line
law of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-sublines-direct}. Fix admissible parameters and a
projective setting with error $\eps$.
Let $D_{\rm dir}$ have mass one and extended-line marginal equal to the line
marginal of the line-point law with coordinate indices sampled uniformly
and directly. Require incidence and affine compatibility with the two source
lines, separate X and Z point marginal mixtures as in Property~2 of
Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-sublines}, and axis-line closure. Its identification with
the seed-indexed law $D$ remains open.

For any paired-line measurement $T$, write $A_{ZX}(T)$ and $A_Z(T)$ for the
ordered-product and Z-point overlap averages displayed in
Lemmas~\ref{lem:claim-17-1}--\ref{lem:claim-17-3}, with $D_{\rm dir}$ in
place of $D$ and a uniform affine parameter on each extended line. Write
$A_Q(Q,T)$ for the joint-point overlap. Line answers are polynomial
representatives of degree at most $md$, evaluations take values in
$\F_q\cup\{\perp\}$, and completed point effects vanish at undefined
evaluations. The placements remain $\mathsf{A}\mathsf{A}'$ and
$\mathsf{B}\mathsf{A}''$.

In the first and third estimates, assume projective joint-point measurements
$Q$ with self-consistency and both opposite-placement ordered-product
squared distances at most $\delta_Q$, and complete paired-line measurements
$T$ with the axis-degree bounds and completed evaluation consistency defect
at most $\delta_P$. These assumptions are not needed in the second estimate,
which uses the concrete sandwich specified there.

